const html = "\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"aside\">\n    <div class=\"aside-logo\"><img class=\"partner-logo-img\" src=\"/images/site/rotaryknk-logo-blue.png\" alt=\"Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club logo\"></div>\n    <div class=\"aside-body\"><p class=\"p\">The Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club is a non-profit service club focused on community service and engagement in the North Kitsap area (Kingston, Hansville, Eglon, Indianola, Suquamish and unincorporated areas of Poulsbo). Over the years, the club has surveyed members of the Kingston and greater North Kitsap communities to identify the most pressing needs and focused their efforts on filling those needs.</p></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"grid4\"><figure class=\"figure\"><img class=\"fig-img\" src=\"/images/site/rotary-flower-baskets.jpg\" alt=\"Rotary volunteers with summer flower baskets\"><figcaption class=\"figcap\">Summer flower baskets</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"figure\"><img class=\"fig-img\" src=\"/images/site/rotary-community-meal.jpg\" alt=\"Rotary volunteers serving a community meal with Kingston Cares\"><figcaption class=\"figcap\">Community meal with Kingston Cares</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"figure\"><img class=\"fig-img\" src=\"/images/site/rotary-bleachers.jpg\" alt=\"Rotary volunteers and a young helper assembling bleachers at a field\"><figcaption class=\"figcap\">Building bleachers</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"figure\"><img class=\"fig-img\" src=\"/images/site/rotary-pavilion.jpg\" alt=\"The Rea Mowery-Kingston Rotary Pavilion with picnic tables\"><figcaption class=\"figcap\">Rea Mowery-Kingston Rotary Pavilion</figcaption></figure></div>\n  <h2 class=\"h2\">Community Contributions</h2>\n  <p class=\"p\">Past initiatives include trail markers in the Heritage Park, lights at the Kingston High School football and track &amp; field, an improved library and community center (Village Green Community Center, Park &amp; Picnic Pavilion), a way to better communicate on-going information (electronic reader board), and middle school field restorations and bleachers.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <h2 class=\"h2\">Addressing Community Needs</h2>\n  <p class=\"p\">For more than twenty years Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club has worked for the betterment of Kingston, Hansville, Indianola, and unincorporated Poulsbo. Each year the Club invests in our community with generous grants to local organizations. We donate to Kingston Cares for summer and holiday food support for school kids, the Kingston Boys and Girls Club, Scouts in Kingston, Kitsap Regional Library for their kids program, Greater Peninsula Conservancy Labs Field Experience for youth, the Kingston Historical Society, and others as needed. We serve up free community meals, too. The summer flower baskets and holiday wreaths adorning Kingston light poles are courtesy of Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <h2 class=\"h2\">Role in the Sports Complex</h2>\n  <p class=\"p\">More than seven years ago, Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club identified a need for more and better-maintained sports fields for area youth. Kids were competing for time and space on unkempt, unlighted muddy fields. Thus began the journey to today. Meeting after meeting led to the ideal centrally-located property now called NKU (North Kitsap United), at Bond Road and Stottlemeyer Road in North Kitsap. The vision soon advanced beyond youth sports, to a fully integrated sports, recreation, and well-being facility for folks of all ages. Ideally, the YMCA of Pierce and Kitsap Counties will be the campus centerpiece. Rotary’s role is now to raise the money necessary to build the sports fields and courts, while the Y will raise money and build its facility.</p>\n  <div class=\"btn-row-left\"><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://www.rotaryknk.org/\">Visit the Kingston North Kitsap Rotary Club website</a></div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"btn-row\"><a class=\"btn btn-gold\" href=\"/donate\">Donate</a><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/get-involved\">Get Involved</a></div>\n";
